id: pm-web-i1mr
title: "pm-web plan routes pass plan-level flags to step subcommands, so adding or editing a plan step never reaches the step"
description: "POST /api/projects/:projectId/pm/plan/:planId/steps sends the step title as --title, but pm plan add-step requires --step-title (exit 2), so every add-step from the web UI fails with a usage error. PATCH /api/projects/:projectId/pm/plan/:planId/steps/:stepRef sends --title/--description, which pm plan update-step silently ignores, so the UI reports success while dropping the user's step edit. Both routes now send --step-title and --step-body."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: bug,http-semantics,pm-plan
created_at: "2026-10-05T04:42:42.911Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-05T05:08:31.439Z"
